    3. Label the event output with identity, order, type, payload, and provenance.
    4. Place reconstruction, validation, readiness, and features in one common core.
    5. Mark outputs as event-level, configuration-level, attempt-level, and item-level tables.
    6. Generate the final diagram from source-controlled code or PreFigure.
    -->
  </subsection>
</section>